# T5 — THE \(w\)-FRAME NOTE

## The cross-frame unit and twisted realized residual, stated once

**RCT unit:** S-4-T5-w-frame  
**Composition pass:** attempt 0/2, 2026-08-12  
**Status:** composed candidate; two clean hostile passes owed  
**Frame of record:** T1, LEMMA GAUGE-COCYCLE, with r1–r3  
**Tower supplier:** certified `[GENTOW5-W(i)]`, read with GENTOW5 S12.1 and the dated \(\psi_j^{(\omega_{j-1})}\) corrigendum

This note gives the cross-frame unit one canonical definition and gives \(\psi^{(w)}\) one home. The former per-note riders become instance records below; they are neither independent definitions nor general laws inferred from measurements.

No absorbed statement changes. GENTOW2 and GENTOW5 remain frozen.

## 1. The \(w\)-inclusive canonical frame

At tower level \(i\), fix the T1 data

\[
K_i,\qquad
N_i:=\widehat n_i(u_{i+1}),\qquad
R_{i+1,\beta},
\]

and

\[
\psi_{i+1}(y)
=
y^{f_{i+1}}-\sum_{t<f_{i+1}}c_ty^t
\in K_i[y].
\]

Put

\[
\bar\kappa_i:=\frac{u_{i+1}}{e(\mu_i)}.
\]

### DEFINITION W-FRAME

The cross-frame unit is

\[
\boxed{
w_i:=
R_{i+1,\bar\kappa_i}
\bigl(\widehat n_i(u_{i+1})\bigr)
\in K_i^\times.
}
\tag{WF-w}
\]

For a monic \(P\in K_i[y]\) of degree \(f\), define

\[
\boxed{
P^{(w_i)}(y):=w_i^fP(y/w_i).
}
\tag{WF-twist}
\]

Thus

\[
\boxed{
\psi_{i+1}^{(w_i)}(y)
=
w_i^{f_{i+1}}\psi_{i+1}(y/w_i)
=
y^{f_{i+1}}
-\sum_{t<f_{i+1}}c_tw_i^{f_{i+1}-t}y^t.
}
\tag{WF-psi}
\]

These are T1’s \(w\)-inclusive canonical definitions. “Cross-frame” means that \(w_i\) converts the multiplicative residual frame to the canonical residual frame. It does not identify \(w_i\) with a separately normalized uniformizer avatar.

Unit substitution preserves monicity, degree, irreducibility, nonzero constant term, and irreducible-factor degrees and multiplicities. Turning factor data into a \(p\)-adic splitting type still requires the surrounding tower theorem.

## 2. The single \(w\)-law

For \(t<f_{i+1}\), put

\[
s_t:=f_{i+1}-t,
\qquad
\beta_t:=s_t\bar\kappa_i,
\]

and use T1’s two telescope orientations

\[
\vartheta_{i,s}
=
\operatorname{res}\!\left(
\frac{\widehat n_i(u_{i+1})^s}
     {\widehat n_i(su_{i+1})}
\right),
\qquad
\Theta_i(t):=\vartheta_{i,s_t}^{-1}.
\]

Define

\[
u_i(\beta_t)
:=
R_{i+1,\beta_t}
\bigl(\widehat n_i(s_tu_{i+1})\bigr).
\]

### LEMMA W-FRAME-LAW

At every certified recipe rung \(2\le i<r\),

\[
\boxed{
u_i(\beta_t)
=
\Theta_i(t)w_i^{s_t}
=
\vartheta_{i,s_t}^{-1}w_i^{s_t}
\qquad(t<f_{i+1}).
}
\tag{WF-law}
\]

The suppliers are:

- \(i=2\): LEMMA GENTOW2-B\(^{\prime\prime}\);
- \(3\le i<r\): the certified companion lemma `[GENTOW5-W(i)]`.

At \(i\ge3\), this is read in the cumulative tower context. Locally, the new assertion at rung \(i\) is `[GENTOW5-W(i)]`; the earlier assertions form the ambient induction history. The certified companion closes that induction from the unconditional \(i=2\) rung.

Per-grade fixedness alone does not prove (WF-law). In particular, this note does not revive S11.2’s withdrawn “\(w\)-blind” argument.

No \(i=1\) version is asserted. S11.3 supplies a fixed letter-power unit there, but its identification with the displayed \(w_1\) remains open.

### Realized-residual corollary

The coherent recipe coefficient is

\[
\Gamma_t=c_t\vartheta_{i,s_t}.
\]

Therefore

\[
\Gamma_tu_i(\beta_t)
=
c_t\vartheta_{i,s_t}
\vartheta_{i,s_t}^{-1}w_i^{s_t}
=
c_tw_i^{s_t},
\]

and hence

\[
\boxed{
R_{\nu_i}(\Phi_{i+1})
=
\psi_{i+1}^{(w_i)}
}
\tag{WF-realized}
\]

at every certified rung \(i\ge2\).

T1 supplies the dictionary and cancellation. GENTOW2-B\(^{\prime\prime}\) or `[GENTOW5-W(i)]` supplies the sitewise B-law.

